                                "sense_id": "974a9a80-1ad2-3f57-bd48-e720f4f7dd8d",
                                "text": "Every little cold gust that I observed in the Colorado country had this corkscrew character […] an auger, of diameter varying from an inch to a thousand feet, capable of altering its direction so as to bore curved holes, revolving with incalculable rapidity, and armed with a cutting edge of silex."
